;; tools/machines-viz's OWN CLJS test lane.
;;
;; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The consolidated `implementation/shadow-cljs.edn`
;; `:node-test` build borrows machines-viz's test tree onto a classpath that
;; spans every artefact, and its `-test$` selector runs every suite here. On
;; that classpath a namespace this artefact forgot to declare still resolves,
;; through some sibling's root. This build compiles the same suites from the
;; artefact's own deps.edn — its own classpath, its own bundle, its own exit
;; code — so what its tests run on is what the artefact declares.
;;
;; Declaring the build HERE also moves the ownership line
;; `scripts/check_test_lane_bijection.py` reads: a source root that stays
;; inside a shadow project is a tree that project's CLJS build OWNS, so rule
;; B2 — "a `.cljc` test on a CLJS-owned root must be selected by a CLJS
;; lane" — holds this tree, where a borrowed root is held by B1 alone.
;;
;; THE SELECTOR IS `-test$` UNDER THE ARTEFACT'S OWN NAMESPACE PREFIX, so a
;; new suite under the prefix is selected on arrival rather than on the audit
;; that finds it. `-dom-cljs-test` namespaces match too and self-gate on
;; `(browser?)` under Node, as they do in the consolidated build. A `.clj`
;; suite is not compiled by shadow-cljs at all: the file extension decides
;; which host runs a test.
;;
;; RUNNING IT: `npm run test:tools-machines-viz` from implementation/.
;; The artefact has no npm surface and needs none — `:js-package-dirs` points
;; shadow-cljs at the one node_modules this repo installs, and the bundle is
;; emitted into implementation/out/ so Node's own upward resolution finds the
;; same tree at run time without a NODE_PATH.
;;
;; `:cljs-test`, not `:test`: shadow-cljs resolves a `:deps {:aliases [...]}`
;; classpath by shelling out to `clojure -A:<alias>`, which INHERITS the
;; alias's `:main-opts` and then hands shadow's own arguments to cognitect's
;; test-runner. The two aliases carry the same test-only deps; `:cljs-test`
;; additionally carries the `page` root, which holds the viewer page entry
;; `viewer_cljs_test.cljs` requires and which the published jar does not ship.
;; See deps.edn.
{:deps {:aliases [:cljs-test]}

 ;; The repo installs exactly one node_modules (implementation/). Pointing at
 ;; it keeps this lane free of a second lockfile to drift against the first.
 :js-options {:js-package-dirs ["../../implementation/node_modules"]}

 :builds
 {:machines-viz-node-test
  {:target    :node-test
   :output-to "../../implementation/out/node-test-tools-machines-viz.js"
   :ns-regexp "^day8\\.re-frame2-machines-viz\\..*-test$"
   ;; The silent-on-success reporter every other lane uses; on the classpath
   ;; via the `day8/re-frame2-test-quiet` :local/root in `:cljs-test`.
   :main      re-frame.test-quiet.shadow-node/main
   ;; The same two suppressions the consolidated `:node-test` build carries and
   ;; for the same reasons: test code redefines freely, and externs inference is
   ;; irrelevant to an un-minified Node run. Warnings-fatal like every
   ;; `:node-test` build there, and nothing else would fail this lane on one:
   ;; `test:tools-machines-viz` compiles through the bare shadow-cljs CLI, and a
   ;; warning in a test namespace still lets the suite pass.
   :compiler-options {:warnings-as-errors true
                      :warnings           {:redef false}
                      :infer-externs      false}}}}
